## Servers

If the OpenAPI spec defines multiple servers, the generated `{{invokerPackage}}\Servers` class exposes each as a `ServerConfiguration` static method (e.g., `Servers::server0()`, `Servers::server1()`, ...) plus a `Servers::all()` array. Pass the desired server's URL to the client:

```php statements
use {{invokerPackage}}\{{clientClassName}};
use {{invokerPackage}}\Servers;

$client = {{clientClassName}}::withToken(Servers::server0()->getUrl(), 'your-token');
```

{{/hasServers}}

## Testing

The `Authenticator` interface is the seam for tests: substitute a fake authenticator that returns a known header map, and assert your code calls the API the way you expect.

```php statements
use {{invokerPackage}}\{{clientClassName}};
use {{invokerPackage}}\Auth\Authenticator;

$fake = new class implements Authenticator {
    public function getHost(): string { return 'https://api.example.com'; }
    public function getAuthHeaders(): array {
        return ['Authorization' => 'Bearer test-token'];
    }
    public function getQueryParams(): array { return []; }
    public function getCookieParams(): array { return []; }
};

$client = new {{clientClassName}}($fake);
```

## Error Handling

An `ApiException` carries `getRequestMethod()` and `getRequestPath()` (no query string) next to `getStatusCode()`.

Every failure the SDK raises derives from `{{errorPrefix}}Exception`; catching it handles them all. It has four direct subtypes: `ApiException` (an HTTP response or transport failure), `SerializationException` (a request or response body that cannot be encoded or decoded), `OAuth2ServerException` (the token endpoint answered with an error) and `OAuth2TokenException` (the token response was unusable). The last two are raised from the first authenticated call, so they are siblings of `ApiException`, not subclasses. The error hierarchy is:

- `{{errorPrefix}}Exception` (root)
  - `SerializationException`
  - `OAuth2ServerException`
  - `OAuth2TokenException`
  - `ApiException`
    - `ClientException` (4xx)
      - `BadRequestException` (400)
      - `UnauthorizedException` (401)
      - `ForbiddenException` (403)
      - `NotFoundException` (404)
      - `ConflictException` (409)
      - `UnprocessableEntityException` (422)
      - `TooManyRequestsException` (429)
      - `PaymentRequiredException` (402)
      - `MethodNotAllowedException` (405)
      - `RequestTimeoutException` (408)
      - `GoneException` (410)
      - `PayloadTooLargeException` (413)
      - `UnsupportedMediaTypeException` (415)
      - `LockedException` (423)
    - `ServerException` (5xx)
      - `InternalServerErrorException` (500)
      - `NotImplementedException` (501)
      - `BadGatewayException` (502)
      - `ServiceUnavailableException` (503)
      - `GatewayTimeoutException` (504)
    - `NetworkException` (no HTTP response, status 0)
      - `NetworkTimeoutException` (the request timed out, status 0)

